  "source_semantics": {
    "claim_supported_by_repository": "The timing authority computes a UTC interval from host before/after monotonic/realtime readings and stores it with receipt.terminal.first_counter; its doc states begin_session starts device sampling before return and treats the first device counter as bounded by those host readings.",
    "current_installed_conclusion": "Current installed PPU source performs a counter-fit refinement, not merely an OPEN bracket: it maps sequence-zero header first_counter through post-OPEN host-bracketed FPGA register reads. This establishes the current code path but not the physical latency/error properties of register reads.",
    "historical_conclusion": "No qualifying artifact binds this current PPU package/version/file hashes to the September capture. The audit therefore makes no historical source-identity claim.",
    "host_adaptive_path": "The host-adaptive wrapper copies upstream start_clock_bracket; after first produced visit it refreshes because its comment says IIO replaces broad OPEN bracket when block zero arrives and can bind the FPGA counter.",
    "interpretation_limit": "Fitted taus are penalized model nuisance parameters coupled to location, selected tracks, catalogue prediction, and per-track CFO. Their seconds-scale values are not a direct measurement of host timestamp error; no timing bug conclusion follows.",
    "unproven_boundary": "This repository exposes the upstream start_clock_bracket as an interface value, but does not contain the lower-level IIO implementation that timestamps OPEN/block zero or proves its bracket bounds receipt.terminal.first_counter after driver/USB buffering. Thus metadata alone cannot establish a physical sample-epoch error bound for this adaptive-IIO generation."
  },
